webOS's file picker.

webOS served a file picker as system UI at
/usr/lib/luna/system/luna-systemui/app/FilePicker/filepicker.html, and enyo.FilePicker (in
Enyo 1) opens exactly that path in an iframe, passing its parameters in the query string and
taking the result back through postMessage. Lunacy serves this page there, so the control
works for every app without any app being changed.

It is Palm's own picker (codepoet, 2026-11-04): its FilePickerApp, with the category list,
photo albums and grid, preview and crop, videos, music and documents, reading the media
index in db8 as on the TouchPad. These are the TouchPad's files, copied unchanged from
/usr/lib/luna/system/luna-systemui on 2026-11-04 (webOS CE 3.1.0):

- palm/: every script app/FilePicker/depends.js loads (FPMainView, AlbumGridView,
  MiscFilePicker, MiscFileItem, AudioPicker, AudioItem, RingtonePicker, ImageAlbumList,
  ImageFullView, ImageCropView, ImagePicker, VideoPicker, VideoAlbumList, FilePickerApp);
- css/: AudioPicker, FilePickerApp, ImageAlbum, ImageAlbumList, ImageAlbumThumbnails,
  MiscFilePicker, RingtoneItem, VideoPicker;
- images/: the folder, whole;
- ../utils/utils.js and ../utils/FileFormatter.js (luna-systemui/utils), which it loads.

Lunacy's own parts:

- filepicker.html: Palm's page, plus one line pointing the page's DbService at Lunacy's relay
  (palm://org.webosarchive.lunacy/media/), which answers db8 reads of the media kinds as the
  system UI, the caller Palm's picker was; and the ringtone type opens the picker below.
- source/RingtonePicker.js: Palm's ringtone picker (FilePickerApp, RingtonePicker and
  AudioPicker) with its list fed from Android's notification sounds through Lunacy's service.
- css/filepicker.css: the page fills its popup, and Palm's three-column photo grid shares a
  popup narrower than its 372 px (a phone's) instead of cutting a column off.
- depends.js: Palm's list, in its order, from palm/, then source/RingtonePicker.js.

